hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"860","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \It is better for a man to fill his belly\nwith oozing pus than to fill it with poetry.\"""""
"861","Al-Aswad ibn Suray' said, \I was a poet and went to the Prophet"
"862","'A'isha said, \Hassan ibn Thabit asked the Messenger of Allah"
"863","Hisham reported that his father said, \I began to abuse Hassan\n[ibn Thabit] in the presence of 'A'isha and she said"
"864","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, said, \Poetry is in the same position as\nspeech. The good of it is like good words and its bad part is like bad\nwords.\"""""
"865","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, said, \Poetry is in the same position as\nspeech. The good of it is like good words and its bad part is like bad\nwords.\"""""
"866","'A'isha said, \Poetry is both good and bad. Take the good and leave\nthe bad. I have related some of the poetry of Ka'b ibn Malik. That included\nan ode of forty verses and some less than that.\"""""
"867","He told us Muhammad bin al-Sabbah, he said: He told us Sharik, from al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, from his father, he said: I said to A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the habit of reciting something from poetry? She said: He was in the habit of reciting something from the poetry of 'Abdullah bin Rawahah: and he would bring you the news of those who had not been provided."
"868","Musa narrated to us, saying: Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan narrated to us, that Al-Aswad ibn Sari' narrated to him, saying: I was a poet. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I have praised my Lord."" He said: ""Indeed, your Lord loves praise,"" and he did not ask me for more than that."
"869","Here is the translated text in English:Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullah bin 'Abd al-Rahman bin Ya'la narrated to us, saying: I heard 'Amr bin al-Sharid, from al-Sharid, saying: The Prophet (peace be upon him) took me to recite the poetry of Umayya bin Abi as-Salt, and I recited it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) then said: ""Hie, hie, until I recited a hundred lines, and then he said: 'It was almost as if he would have become Muslim.'"""
"870","Ibn 'Umar reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \It is better for one of you to fill his belly with pus\nthan to fill it with poetry.\"""""
"871","He informed us, Ali bin al-Husayn, he said: My father informed me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: ""And the poets are followed by the foolish ones"" until he said ""And they say what they do not do"", then he erased that and specified, saying ""Except for those who have believed"" until he said ""They will return""."
"872","Ibn 'Abbas said that a man - or a bedouin - came to the\nProphet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and spoke some eloquent\nwords. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \There\nis some magic eloquence and some wisdom in poetry.\"""""
"873","'Abdu'l-Malik ibn Marwan entrusted the teaching of his children\nto ash-Sha'bi and said, \Teach them poetry so that they will possess dignity\nand vigor. Feed them meat so that their hearts will be strong. Cut off\ntheir hair so that their necks will be strong. Make them sit with men of\ndistinction who will contradict them in words.\"""""
"874","'A'isha reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \The greatest of criminals is the poet who satirises the\nentire tribe and a man who disclaims his father.\"""""
"875","Ibn 'Umar said, \Two men came from the east as orators in the time\nof the Messenger of Allah"
"876","Anas said, \A man gave a speech in the presence of 'Umar and said\na lot. 'Umar said"
"877","Abu Yazid or Ma'n ibn Yazid reported that the Prophet, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, said, \Gather in your mosques. When the\npeople are gathered"
"878","He told us Khalid bin Makhlad, he said: He told us Sulaiman bin Bilal, he said: He told us Yahya bin Sa'id, he said: I heard 'Abdullah bin 'Amir bin Rabee'ah saying: 'A'isha said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""I wish there was a righteous man from my companions who would come to me and guard me tonight, for when we heard the sound of the silah, we said, 'Who is this?' He said, 'Sa'd, O Messenger of Allah, I have come to guard you.' Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) fell asleep until we heard his snoring."""
